.TH CTRL-EXEC-API 8 "2026-06-10" "ctrl-exec" "ctrl-exec Manual"
.SH NAME
ctrl-exec-api \- HTTP API server for ctrl-exec
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ctrl-exec-api
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ctrl-exec-api
exposes the ctrl-exec run, ping, discovery, and status operations over HTTP
on the control host. It reads its configuration from
.B ctrl-exec.conf
and uses the same auth hook as the CLI. By default it binds to
.I 127.0.0.1
on port 7445; set
.B api_bind
and
.B api_port
in the configuration to change this. The hook is read at startup, so
restart the service after changing it.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-\-config " path"
Path to
.BR ctrl-exec.conf .
Default:
.IR /etc/ctrl-exec-dispatcher/ctrl-exec.conf .
.SH CONFIGURATION
Relevant keys in
.BR ctrl-exec.conf :
.TP
.B api_socket
Unix socket path for same-host callers (optional), created mode 0660.
Can run beside the TCP listener.
.TP
.B api_socket_group
Group of the socket file (default: the server's own group).
.TP
.B api_port
TCP port to listen on (default 7445);
.B off
for no TCP listener (then
.B api_socket
is required).
.TP
.B api_bind
Bind address (default 127.0.0.1).
.TP
.B api_tls_cert ", " api_tls_key
TLS certificate and key for the TCP listener (plain HTTP if neither is set).
Setting only one, or an unreadable file, is refused.
.TP
.B auth_hook
Auth hook executable.
.TP
.B auth_deny_generic
When set, denied requests return a generic 403 without the specific reason.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 78
Configuration refused: no listener, an incomplete or unreadable TLS pair, an
unknown socket group, or an old
.I /etc/ctrl-exec
directory.
.PP
Confidential run input should only be sent over the unix socket or TLS.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ctrl-exec-dispatcher (8),
.BR ctrl-exec-agent (8).
.PP
Full HTTP API reference: the API document shipped with ctrl-exec and
.UR https://github.com/OpenDigitalCC/ctrl-exec
.UE .
